{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Behold, He empties.</b> Like \"empties,\" and like it \"a vine emptied\" (Nahum 2:10)." "<b>and laid waste.</b> In the sense of \"devastates,\" and the cognate of this word [occurs] in this book." "<b>and distorts.</b> He turns its face."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:51.518731885Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}